WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.160
- It's giving Tuesday tomorrow, everyone,

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.470
which is one reason why we are very happy

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.330
to have our first guest here today.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.700
You may know him best as
an award-winning actor

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.130
and musician, but he's also got a podcast

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.900
where he talks with
people about giving back

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.460
and changing the world for the better.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.500
It's called "Six Degrees
with Kevin Bacon".

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.330
You can listen wherever
you get your podcasts.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.631
Everybody, give it up for Kevin Bacon.

00:00:20.631 --> 00:00:24.388
(audience yells and claps)

00:00:24.388 --> 00:00:27.471
(band music playing)

00:00:37.123 --> 00:00:38.940
Oh my gosh, you're in a band.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.773
You get that.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:42.483
Do you just get up on stage
sometimes and go, huh?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.020
- Yeah, I do oftentimes.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.300
And I have to say, I love this outfit.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.215
- [Kelly] Oh, thank you.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.130
- It's so good.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.335
- [Kelly] Thank you.

00:00:51.335 --> 00:00:52.276
(audience cheering)

00:00:52.276 --> 00:00:53.109
- Can I say that?

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:53.942
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:53.942 --> 00:00:58.942
- It reminds me of the 1968
Elvis Comeback Special.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:00:59.900
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:00.837
- Have you ever seen that?

00:01:00.837 --> 00:01:03.300
- No, but anytime I remind
someone of the king,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.835
I'm totally cool with that.

00:01:04.835 --> 00:01:08.620
- Let me tell you, watch the
1968 Elvis Comeback Special.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.461
- Okay, I should've done a move.

00:01:10.461 --> 00:01:12.720
- And he's basically, he's
basically copying your style.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.852
- Yeah, back to the future, there we go.

00:01:15.852 --> 00:01:17.430
But you, I just moved here.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.460
So you first moved here awhile
back, but what was it like?

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.410
- 1976 I moved here.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.599
- [Kelly] Did you love it?

00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:24.600
- I loved it, yeah.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.108
I grew up in Philly, and um.

00:01:27.108 --> 00:01:29.139
- [Kelly] That's not far, yeah, yeah.

00:01:29.139 --> 00:01:30.046
- Yeah, it's not far.

00:01:30.046 --> 00:01:31.890
I'd been here a few times
because my sister lived here.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.100
My sister lived on West End Avenue,

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.200
so she was very nice to
let me sleep on her couch

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.200
for probably, I don't know, four months

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.926
until I got my feet on the ground, yeah.

00:01:42.926 --> 00:01:43.796
- That's nice.

00:01:43.796 --> 00:01:45.293
Yeah, because it's not a cheap city, no.

00:01:45.293 --> 00:01:48.291
- No, no, although I can
tell you that in 1976,

00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:53.291
my budget for my apartment
was $150 a month.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.040
- So you lived in a closet.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.596
- Right, well.

00:01:57.596 --> 00:01:58.718
- [Kelly] Of someone else's.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.330
- Someone else's closet.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:03.660
Well, what happened was
I had figured it was 150,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.280
I don't know where I got the math on that,

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.920
but that's what I had decided.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.340
- Yeah.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.640
- And so I went into this,
I saw an ad in the back

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.470
of the "Village Voice", and it said,

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.310
artists, actors, musicians, residents.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.440
And I thought, well that sounds good.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.843
It was basically a flop
house, really, I mean.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.830
I don't know, I guess there
were some artists there,

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.030
but not a lot.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.850
- Like do you mind living with rats?

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.900
- Exactly, yeah, exactly.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.240
But I walked into the rental office,

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.740
and the guy said, no, we don't have any

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.740
single room apartments, but we
do have a two-room apartment.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.350
So basically it was a
kitchen and another room.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.160
And I said, he said that's
three and a quarter a month,

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.440
and I said I can't afford that
and I don't have a roommate.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.060
And he said, what about this guy?

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.610
I'm sitting on the couch and
I look, I don't know this guy,

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.674
and he goes, you want to live together?

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:56.507
And I was like, yeah, okay.

00:02:56.507 --> 00:02:58.290
Yeah, okay, we'll live together.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.630
Yeah, and we lived
together for four years.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.690
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:04.593
- Yeah, in fact I just had
lunch with him the other day.

00:03:06.514 --> 00:03:07.624
- What?

00:03:07.624 --> 00:03:09.453
- And he was a classical pianist.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.270
- You were both musicians,
yeah, that's cool.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:16.756
- Yeah, he was great,
great, played beautifully.

00:03:16.756 --> 00:03:18.810
You know, in the middle of the afternoon,

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.733
he worked nights at the Copa Cabana,

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.068
and in the middle of the afternoon.

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:25.203
- This is a TV show, what?

00:03:26.332 --> 00:03:28.710
- Yeah, yeah, he'd come home,

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.200
and he'd be playing Chopin or whatever.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.970
It was really cool.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:33.803
- That's incredible.

00:03:33.803 --> 00:03:35.850
I actually moved out to
LA with some random person

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:36.720
I did not know.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:37.839
- Really?

00:03:37.839 --> 00:03:38.672
- Yeah, she just needed a roommate.

00:03:38.672 --> 00:03:39.634
I was like, I'll do it.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:43.397
And I moved from Texas
to LA with a stranger.

00:03:43.397 --> 00:03:45.120
- Wow, and how long did that last?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.680
- Not long, we moved into a place,

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.270
and it burnt down.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.430
So yeah, then I slept
in my car for a few days

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.050
and then tried out for a
show called "American Idol".

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.772
So it all worked out.

00:03:53.772 --> 00:03:56.684
(audience cheering)

00:03:56.684 --> 00:03:58.157
Yeah, life, yeah.

00:03:58.157 --> 00:04:00.930
I feel like everyone in this
industry has some crazy thing

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.730
where you've either lived in your car

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.800
or on a mattress in
someone's house or yeah,

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.840
it's like, yeah, you really
gotta want your dream.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:09.240
- You do, you gotta have the hunger.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.820
- Yeah, the universe
makes you really want it.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.890
But you played with Billy
Joel in Madison Square Garden.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:14.913
That is incredible.

00:04:15.802 --> 00:04:16.930
- I did, yeah, it was amazing.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.849
- [Kelly] I would love to do that.

00:04:18.849 --> 00:04:19.682
(audience clapping)

00:04:19.682 --> 00:04:20.515
Were you nervous?

00:04:20.515 --> 00:04:21.348
- Oh my God, what, are you kidding me?

00:04:21.348 --> 00:04:23.730
Of course, of course I was nervous, yeah.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.050
- I wouldn't have been
nervous about the audience.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.520
I would have been nervous about him.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.883
- Well, yeah, I mean listen,

00:04:28.883 --> 00:04:32.280
you know it's one of those
moments where you look at the,

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.690
they sent me the set list,

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.640
and I looked at the set
list, and I was like,

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:40.640
oh wow, every single one of
the songs on this set list

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.920
is like a massive hit.
- Is like a massive hit.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:44.753
Yeah.

00:04:44.753 --> 00:04:47.610
- It was just a weird thing
because I'm a Billy Joel fan,

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.290
but I never met Billy.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.673
We didn't know each other.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:55.110
And he reached out to say did Kira and I

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:55.980
want to come to the show?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.810
And I said, yeah, of
course, and we were like,

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:58.680
wow, that's awesome.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.820
Billy Joel was, we can go
to the show at the Garden.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.890
And then about a week later, it was like,

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:07.140
do you want to come to the
show and also do a song?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:07.990
I was like, what?

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:13.290
It was literally if I could,
it was like, you know.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.520
- Yeah, and then grab tequila, yeah.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.570
- Grab tequila.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.760
- You're like, wait,
what about this decision?

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.120
- I had the tequila
ready for after the show.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.953
- [Kelly] For after.

00:05:21.953 --> 00:05:23.358
- Yes.

00:05:23.358 --> 00:05:24.330
- That was probably smart,
that was a smart decision.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.830
- Yeah, so it was really fun.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.110
- But you're not just, you
just got honored in Philly.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.420
You got a...

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.253
- Yeah, my brother and I.

00:05:30.253 --> 00:05:31.715
- You got the walk of
fame, that's so cool.

00:05:31.715 --> 00:05:33.943
(audience cheering)

00:05:33.943 --> 00:05:35.243
That's amazing.

00:05:35.243 --> 00:05:37.800
Leslie Odom Junior was
just here like a week ago.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:38.633
He got that too.

00:05:38.633 --> 00:05:39.466
- [Kevin] That's right.

00:05:39.466 --> 00:05:40.299
- [Kelly] Yeah, he's from Philly as well.

00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:41.132
- [Kevin] Yeah, yeah.

00:05:41.132 --> 00:05:42.210
- [Kelly] That's prestigious, yeah.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.910
- Well listen, I mean Philadelphia

00:05:44.889 --> 00:05:46.414
has an amazing music tradition.

00:05:46.414 --> 00:05:47.370
- [Kelly] Yeah, Pink's from Philly too.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.724
- Yeah, Pink.

00:05:48.724 --> 00:05:50.295
- There's a lot of good
people coming out of there.

00:05:50.295 --> 00:05:52.282
(audience cheering)

00:05:52.282 --> 00:05:53.569
Congratulations.

00:05:53.569 --> 00:05:56.010
- John Oates, I mean, and just
the sound of Philadelphia,

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.290
all those, you know,
Kenny Gamble, Leon Huff,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.910
all those great song writers.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.550
And it was really cool.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.960
I mean this is a street that, you know,

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.210
is only a few blocks
from where I grew up, so.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:08.250
- Wow, that makes it more special.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.321
- Yeah definitely.

00:06:09.321 --> 00:06:10.982
- That's really cool, awesome.

00:06:10.982 --> 00:06:14.779
(band music playing)

00:06:14.779 --> 00:06:15.612
All right you all.

00:06:15.612 --> 00:06:17.352
We are back with Kevin Bacon.

00:06:17.352 --> 00:06:18.506
Give it up.

00:06:18.506 --> 00:06:19.797
(audience cheering)

00:06:19.797 --> 00:06:21.450
Kevin actually plays a few instruments

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.650
and just learned another,
so let's see that.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.090
- This is called pig
belly, it goes like this.

00:06:28.036 --> 00:06:31.036
(hands patting pig)

00:06:38.075 --> 00:06:39.699
(audience cheering)

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:41.050
- Like first of all, we
didn't show the beginning,

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.710
where you're kind of
rubbing against her hair.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.675
- Yeah.

00:06:44.675 --> 00:06:45.720
- That was also nice, the sound.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.130
It was like a little washboard.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.390
Do you usually play on pigs?

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:52.535
- Yeah, he has very, very,
is very bristly, yeah.

00:06:52.535 --> 00:06:53.368
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:53.368 --> 00:06:55.590
- He sounds great, that
pig, he really does.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:57.570
- Well speaking of pigs,
something just happened

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:00.307
in Kevin's home state that
had a lot of people worried.

00:07:00.307 --> 00:07:01.890
Here are some headlines.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:04.140
Kevin Bacon, the pig, not the actor,

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.750
missing after PA barn escape.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.060
Kevin Bacon remains on
the run in central PA.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.460
It feels like I'm on SNL right now.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.830
An escaped pet pig named Kevin Bacon

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.320
is becoming an internet sensation.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.960
I heard you actually
helped find Kevin Bacon.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:21.930
- Well, I didn't help find Kevin Bacon.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.066
- [Kelly] With a flashlight, and yeah.

00:07:24.066 --> 00:07:26.340
- No, I pointed out that he was missing.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.890
- I know, but you have a
lot of followers, so yeah.

00:07:29.763 --> 00:07:32.610
- Well I don't know, if I
was helpful, I'm thrilled.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:36.000
- Yeah, it's a great name
for a pig, it's amazing.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.237
- Yeah, it is.

00:07:37.237 --> 00:07:38.070
- I'm mad I never thought of it.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.780
We had a pig, named her Sadie.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.605
We should have named it Kevin Bacon.

00:07:41.605 --> 00:07:42.438
(audience laughing)

00:07:42.438 --> 00:07:43.726
- Yeah.

00:07:43.726 --> 00:07:45.810
- But we have a family
member of Kevin Bacon pig

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:46.950
in our audience.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.780
Everybody meet Chelsea.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.229
What's up, Chelsea?

00:07:50.229 --> 00:07:52.469
(audience clapping)

00:07:52.469 --> 00:07:54.720
So, you found the pig, right?

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.520
- We found the pig, we found the bacon.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.830
- [Kelly] Did you find
out where Kevin Bacon was?

00:07:58.830 --> 00:07:59.663
- So.

00:07:59.663 --> 00:08:00.633
- Was he in a barn dancing?

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.800
- He did wonder close to the
barn, but there was no dancing.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.710
- Okay, disappointment,
all right, all right.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:08.580
How did the pig get home?

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.530
How did you end up figuring it out?

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:14.040
- So, he was on the land for
about two and a half weeks,

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.150
and you know, we had shared
on social media about it

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:22.320
because I didn't want the
local hunters to find my pig

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.610
and make a mistake.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:24.647
- Yeah.

00:08:24.647 --> 00:08:27.370
- So we put it online,
and then Kevin Bacon human

00:08:28.391 --> 00:08:31.770
shared the story about Kevin Bacon pig,

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:34.650
and honestly, it was such.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.360
- How many times do you
think we'll say Kevin Bacon

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.193
in this episode?

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:39.393
- A million.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.550
It was really renewed hope when
Kevin Bacon human shared it.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:45.960
It was getting a little
rough in the trenches,

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.900
and you know, the next thing we knew

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.690
somebody was suggesting
that I put out donuts

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.130
for Kevin Bacon pig.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.650
So I didn't have donuts,
but I got sticky buns

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.540
and pet-safe Benadryl.

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:58.380
- Yeah.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.790
I love that you said pet-safe.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.696
You're like, don't attack me, people.

00:09:01.696 --> 00:09:04.563
- Yeah, I took a bite out
of it first, it's fine.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.200
- Yeah, and he took a nap.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.930
- Yes, he wondered on in sleepily,

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.180
and now he's home forever and safe.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.050
- Aw, that's sweet.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.183
I love, pets are our family.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.757
- Yes, you know what's interesting is that

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:24.810
my wife often uses sticky buns
and Benadryl to lure me in.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:28.303
- This is, to get you to go to sleep.

00:09:28.303 --> 00:09:30.360
I have so many jokes that
aren't daytime right now,

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.193
it's funny.

